Note: a4.db-wal is 16,512 bytes — this database has writes
  nothing has checkpointed, so something probably has it open (the dev server), or something exited
  without closing it. Stop `npm run dev` first if you can: with another connection open, copying the
  backup back over the database afterwards does not take effect, and can corrupt it (Round 191).
  Running anyway — this is a warning, not a refusal, because a WAL left by a crash looks the same.

